<title>MOROCCO: France lends Morocco $39.2 mln for rural electricity.</title>
<headline>France lends Morocco $39.2 mln for rural electricity.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>A French fund said on Wednesday it provided Morocco with 220 million French francs ($39.2 million) in financial aid to bring electricity to 336 villages.</p>
<p>Olivier Beugnot, director of the Caisse Francaise de Developpement (CFD) in Morocco told reporters that the fund had contributed 125 million francs to clean up the central city of Fez plagued by industrial pollution.</p>
<p>He said the fund planned other actions in the same line in Rabat and the southern city of Agadir.</p>
<p>Beugnot added that Morocco came first on the list of CFD recipients with 2.6 billion francs for the period between 1992 and 1996.</p>
<p>CFD's loans are guaranteed by the French government.</p>
</text>
